Different failures can require different responses.

```java
try {
    int index = Integer.parseInt(input);
    System.out.println(values[index]);
} catch (NumberFormatException e) {
    System.out.println("Please enter an integer.");
} catch (ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
    System.out.println("That index is outside the array.");
}
```

Java checks the `catch` blocks in order and uses the first compatible one.

More specific exception types should generally appear before more general ones.

Because it is often too broad.

This:

```java
