Once that meaning is clear, the recursive structure becomes easier:

```java
public static boolean contains(
        int[] values,
        int target,
        int index) {

    if (index == values.length) {
        return false;
    }

    if (values[index] == target) {
        return true;
    }

    return contains(values, target, index + 1);
}
```

A clear method meaning helps you determine:

- the correct base case,
- the smaller recursive problem,
- what result the recursive call represents.

