```java
public static int sum(int[] values) {
    return sum(values, 0);
}

private static int sum(int[] values, int index) {
    if (index == values.length) {
        return 0;
    }

    return values[index] + sum(values, index + 1);
}
```

The public method provides the convenient interface.

The private helper carries the extra parameter required for recursion.

This is a common and useful design pattern.

